		<label>Type 56-1 (Drum)</label>
		<description>Caliber: 7.62x39mm. 75-round detachable mag. Select-Fire.
		
The Type 56 is a Chinese copy of the Soviet Avtomat Kalashnikov (AK) rifle. Though almost a 1:1 copy of the Type III AK, the Type 56 has some notable differences - notably, most are found with stamped (like on the AKM) rather than milled receivers, and the Type 56 has a distinctive enclosed hooded front sight. Type 56 rifles also often feature their own integral folding bayonets. Chinese AKs are among the most common in the world today, Type 56 rifles in their original configuration are still produced.

This variant is a Type 56-1, a copy of the AKS rifle which features an underfolding stock.</description>
